;; The reaper checked against its Rocq transcriptions: for each example X.fl,
;; after Simplify, the compiler's reaper and the transcriptions extracted from
;; middle_end/flambda2/rocq/reaper/FlambdaReaper*.v are run on the same unit,
;; and the graphs, the solutions and the rebuilt terms are compared (see
;; ../../tools/flreaper.ml). What the tool prints is kept in X.expected,
;; beside X.fl; a difference that it finds is printed and kept there too. The
;; tool fails only when the solution it computes for the model's graph does
;; not pass the extracted checks.
;;
;; To add an example, add X.fl (its module symbol must match its name) and
;; X.expected, and nothing else: `dune promote` writes X.expected. Each
;; example is run on its own, as the compiler keeps its symbols from one unit
;; to the next.
;;
;; The rules are made from the .fl files that are here by gen_rules.sh, and
;; included by run/dune, as in the directory above.

(rule
 (deps
  (glob_files *.fl)
  (glob_files *.expected))
 (action
  (with-stdout-to
   dune.inc
   (run sh %{dep:gen_rules.sh} %{deps}))))
